course: dictionary
lesson: 9058
title: Sleeveless
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are easy to picture when you look at their parts. Sleeveless is made of two parts: sleeve, the part of a top that covers your arm, and -less, which means without. So sleeveless means without sleeves.
explain: A sleeveless top, shirt or dress has no sleeves, so your arms are bare from the shoulder down. Writers use this word for clothes in stories and everyday life, especially summer clothes and sports kit. It tells you the weather is warm or the person is active.
explain: Read this sentence from Alice's story: «a watch out of its waistcoat-pocket». The text then says a waistcoat is a sleeveless jacket worn over a shirt. The clue is in the word itself: sleeve plus less means no sleeves.
fact: Sleeveless means having no sleeves.
fact: Sleeve is the part of a top that covers your arm, and -less means without.
fact: You can say a sleeveless top, a sleeveless vest, a sleeveless dress or a sleeveless jumper (UK).
fact: «A waistcoat is a sleeveless jacket worn over a shirt.»
fact: A sleeveless top often means warm weather or a sporty day.
exercise: The text says a waistcoat is a sleeveless jacket worn over a shirt. What does sleeveless mean? | Made of wool | Worn only in winter | *Having no sleeves | Having very long sleeves
exercise: Mia wears a sleeveless top to football practice on a hot day. Why might she choose it? | So she can stay warm in the snow | *So her arms are free and cool in the warm weather | So she can hide in the crowd | So her arms are covered from the shoulder down
exercise: Find and copy the word that means having no sleeves. | *sleeveless | jacket | sleeve | waistcoat
test: Which of these is a sleeveless top? | A pair of warm gloves | A jumper with long sleeves | *A sleeveless vest | A coat with a hood
test: Sam wore a sleeveless jumper in the sun. What does this tell you? | It was snowing | *It was warm | It was dark and cold | It was raining hard
exam: Lily put on a ___ dress for the summer party. | Hooded | Woolly | *Sleeveless | Frozen
